course: dictionary
lesson: 6614
title: Finding the northeast
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A compass has four main points: north, east, south and west. Northeast sits exactly between north and east, so it is a direction you can name like the others. Picture a clock: north is at twelve and east is at three, so northeast is the spot in between, at about half past one.
explain: On a map with north at the top, northeast is the top-right corner. Read the clues: if north is up and east is right, then northeast is up and to the right. Check by pointing your finger up and to the right.
explain: The word can also name a part of a place. «Puyi ... was made ruler of Manchukuo, a state in the northeast» tells you the northeast is one part of a larger country. The words «in the northeast» show that it is an area, not just a direction.
explain: Northeast can describe things that move or come from that way. «The Qing dynasty ... was founded by the Manchus from the northeast» means they came from that direction. A northeast wind blows from the northeast. Some people also write it as north-east, and it means the same thing.
fact: Northeast is one of the eight main compass points: N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W, NW.
fact: Northeast is halfway between north and east, 45 degrees from each.
fact: On a map with north at the top, northeast is the top-right corner.
fact: «In the northeast» means in the part of an area that faces that direction.
fact: A «northeast wind» is a wind that blows from the northeast.
fact: Northeast can also be written «north-east», and both spellings mean the same direction.
exercise: Which direction is halfway between north and east? | *Northeast | South | Southeast | West
exercise: On a map with north at the top, where is the northeast? | Top-left corner | Bottom-left corner | Middle of the map | *Top-right corner
exercise: «The Qing dynasty ... was founded by the Manchus from the northeast.» Where did the Manchus come from? | The west | *The northeast | The south | The sea
test: What does a «northeast wind» do? | It blows from the west | It is always still | *It blows from the northeast | It blows only at night
test: Northeast lies between which two directions? | East and west | *North and east | South and west | North and south
exam: Ella says «north-east» is a different direction from «northeast». Who is right? | Nobody knows, because compasses have no northeast | *Ella is wrong, because both spellings mean the same direction | Ella, because the hyphen changes the meaning | Ella is right, because north-east is further away
